azis are aware of the tiles  capabilities and they're already looking  for more elsewhere in Europe and there  may well be more out there the lab might  be destroyed but the search for the  substance I can grant a thousand-year  Reich is definitely not it's clear from  what little we know of the Nazis actual  scientific process that there's been a  lot of trial and error involved in this  serum they're developing and we don't  actually know how they realize they  could use a tar beneath the church for  that purpose in the first place  Overlord is a film that plays on reports  of secret Nazi programs geared towards  all sorts of occult things so the film  can get away with a lot this atmosphere  plus the strange dead animal the  soldiers discover in the woods hints  that there were definitely experiments  of a different kind in this village  before the serum was developed was the  doctor up to some kind of gene splicing  was he trying to create hybrid war dogs  of some kind we don't know but the Nazis  sloppy operation implies that there's  more to be found out there than just  human zombies Overlord takes as many  genre liberties as at once  but it also follows certain war movie  structural conventions and perhaps  nowhere is that more evident than in the  story of Chloe and her little brother  Paul who bond with the soldiers after  they holed up in their house a romantic  connection between boys and Chloe is  heavily implied what happens now do the  soldiers just move on and leave these  two to be build their lives they might  be separated temporarily but the bonding  experience of the mission and boys his  sensitive soul makes them being apart  permanently seem unlikely he might march  on to Berlin sure but we feel like he'll  be back eventually to get to know the  French girl a little better at the  beginning of overlord Ford is the rough  cynical officer who's been through hell  and isn't about to go soft for anyone  while boys is the innocent young trainee  who's terrified of war and once proved  himself too sensitive to even kill a  mouse by the end of the film  Ford is dead and boys  absorbed many of his lessons he's  capable of killing a thinking on his  feet and winning in a hard fights even  if much of his innocence and compassion  have been preserved we get the sense of  boys isn't likely to just leave chloe in  the village forever but what about the  rest of his military career if the film  adheres to the same World War two  timeline as the real world then boys  still has nearly a year of fighting left  to do and then he might be left in  Europe to clean up after the Nazis when  Germany surrenders he's had experience  with the supernatural now even if he's  not telling anyone about it will he just  leave that in his past or will he be  keeping an eye open for other Nazi  facilities like the one beneath the  church ready to strike as necessary  we're betting on the latter
 

